        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>Dropping cable or satellite TV isn\u2019t the only way to lower your TV bill.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Even if you\u2019re not ready to cut the cord, you may still be able to find some extra savings through your current pay TV provider. By renting less equipment, bundling some streaming services, and making sure you\u2019re not overpaying for internet, you can save decent money while hanging onto cable\u2019s creature comforts.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>While switching to streaming or over-the-air TV will likely be cheaper in the long run, here are some other ways to reduce your TV bill before you make the leap:</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"return-your-cable-boxes-and-stream-instead\">Return your cable boxes and stream instead</h2>\n\n\n<div class=\"extendedBlock-wrapper block-coreImage undefined\"><figure data-wp-context='{\"imageId\":\"6a2c03639b17e\"}' data-wp-interactive=\"core/image\" class=\"wp-block-im",
